{
  "description": "How extraction/measure_section_heights.mjs maps rendered DOM regions to section ids at 1440px. Free block templates (product, compare and company block pages) map the children of <main> one-to-one onto the route's blockOrder in templates/routes.json. Every other template lists its non-chrome sections here in page order; the promo bar (#root > :nth-child(1)), nav (#root > nav) and footer (#root > footer) come from the template chrome. Parallel columns that a grid stretches to the row height (careers.sidebar, story.sidebar) are measured by their content extent, not by the stretched box. The optional tag field names the section's root element when the measured box is an inner wrapper. Entry kinds: el = one element; from+to = vertical extent from the top of one element to the bottom of another; each = every match is one instance; mode = special splitter (manifesto). optional entries are skipped when absent.",
  "viewport": { "width": 1440, "height": 900 },
  "basePath": "/en-GB",
  "templates": {
    "template.home": [
      { "section": "home.hero", "el": "main > :nth-child(1)" },
      { "section": "home.awards", "el": "main > :nth-child(2)" },
      { "section": "home.product-overview", "el": "main > :nth-child(3)" },
      { "section": "home.feature-carousel", "el": "main > :nth-child(4)" },
      { "section": "home.agents", "el": "main > :nth-child(5)" },
      { "section": "home.stats", "el": "main > :nth-child(6)" },
      { "section": "home.mission", "el": "main > :nth-child(7)" },
      { "section": "home.content-cards", "el": "main > :nth-child(8)" },
      { "section": "home.logo-marquee", "el": "main > :nth-child(9)" }
    ],
    "template.customers-index": [
      { "section": "customers.hero", "el": "main > :nth-child(1)" },
      { "section": "customers.logo-grid", "el": "main > :nth-child(2)" },
